{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MotivesArchimedean","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MotivesArchimedean","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic"],"declarations":33,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.VolThroughTau.factors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.VolThroughTau.factors","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L159-L159","doc":"Factorization equation: `knotVol = τ_arch(algVol)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.VolThroughTau.knotVol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.VolThroughTau.knotVol","kind":"def","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L157-L157","doc":"The real-valued knot volume of the braid closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.VolThroughTau.algVol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.VolThroughTau.algVol","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L155-L155","doc":"The algebraic quantum volume of a braid (as an object of `C`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.VolThroughTau.τ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.VolThroughTau.τ","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L153-L153","doc":"The QOU fibre functor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.VolThroughTau.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.VolThroughTau.mk","kind":"ctor","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L151-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.VolThroughTau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.VolThroughTau","kind":"structure","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L145-L159","doc":"**Vol(K) factors strictly through `τ`.**\n\nThe real-valued knot volume of a braid closure equals the\n`τ_arch`-image of its algebraic quantum volume. This is the\nQOU statement of the volume conjecture as a *factorization*\nthrough the unique fibre functor `τ : C → Arch`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.realize","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.realize","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L141-L141","doc":"Real-valued realization `R_top : Motive → ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.archPostProc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.archPostProc","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L139-L139","doc":"Real-valued archimedean post-processing map (`π_∞` after the\n`ℤ → ℝ` cast of the Euler characteristic). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.eulerChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.eulerChar","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L136-L136","doc":"Topological Euler characteristic `χ_top : M̂ → ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.Motive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.Motive","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L134-L134","doc":"Source: the dimension-completion `M̂` of the Grothendieck ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor.mk","kind":"ctor","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L132-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanRealizationFunctor","kind":"structure","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L113-L141","doc":"The **archimedean realization** `R_top` (a motivic measure, NOT a\nfunctor).\n\nDespite the historical name, this is a map *out of the Grothendieck\nring* `M̂` — `eulerChar` is a ring homomorphism (a motivic measure)\nand the archimedean post-processing is a place — so it has no action\non morphisms and is not a `CategoryTheory.Functor`. The genuine\nfunctor is `FibreFunctor` (τ) above; `R_top` agrees with `τ_arch`\n(the object-level evaluation `π_∞ ∘ τ`) on QOU motivic data.\n\nMaps a motivic class to `ℝ` via the topological Euler\ncharacteristic followed by an archimedean post-processing map.\nThe archimedean projection `π_∞ : 𝔸 → ℝ` of the adelic\nsubstrate is, in this formalization, applied as the\nreal-valued post-processing map `archPostProc : ℝ → ℝ` on the\nEuler characteristic (cast to `ℝ`); the full adelic-carrier\ntarget lives in `QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.AdelicSubstrate`.\nOn QOU motivic data this composite agrees with `τ_arch`\n(`prop:vol-through-tau`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:archimedean-realization-functor","label":"def:archimedean-realization-functor","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-realization-functor.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.FibreFunctor.archRestriction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.FibreFunctor.archRestriction","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L106-L111","doc":"The archimedean restriction `τ_arch = π_∞ ∘ τ` of a fibre functor,\nderived from `τ.functor` and `Arch.archProj`. A plain function\n`C → ℝ` — the object-level archimedean evaluation, not a functor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.FibreFunctor.functor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.FibreFunctor.functor","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L104-L104","doc":"The underlying genuine functor `τ : C ⥤ Arch.Obj`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.FibreFunctor.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.FibreFunctor.mk","kind":"ctor","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.FibreFunctor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.FibreFunctor","kind":"structure","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L93-L104","doc":"The QOU **fibre functor** `τ`, a genuine `C ⥤ Arch.Obj`.\n\nThis is a genuine `CategoryTheory.Functor`: it carries an action on\nobjects (`τ.functor.obj`) **and** on morphisms (`τ.functor.map`),\nsatisfying the functor laws. The archimedean restriction\n`τ_arch = π_∞ ∘ τ : C → ℝ` is *derived* (see\n`FibreFunctor.archRestriction` below) — it composes the functor `τ`\nwith the object-level evaluation `Arch.archProj` and so is NOT\nitself a functor (its codomain `ℝ` is a set/ring, not a category). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory.archProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory.archProj","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L89-L89","doc":"Real-valued evaluation `π_∞ : Obj → ℝ` on the archimedean place\n(object-level; not functorial). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory.cat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory.cat","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L86-L86","doc":"The category structure on `Arch` — morphisms, composition,\nidentities. This is what makes `τ : C ⥤ Arch.Obj` a genuine functor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory.Obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory.Obj","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L83-L83","doc":"Carrier type of objects in `Arch`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory.mk","kind":"ctor","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L81-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ArchimedeanCategory","kind":"structure","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L70-L89","doc":"An abstract **archimedean target category** `Arch`.\n\nThe codomain of the QOU fibre functor. `Arch` is a *bundle*: it\ncarries a genuine category on its object type `Arch.Obj` (via the\n`[Category Obj]` instance below), so the fibre functor is concretely\n`τ : C ⥤ Arch.Obj`. Each object also exposes a real-valued\narchimedean evaluation `archProj : Obj → ℝ`.\n\nNote `archProj` is an **object-level evaluation** (`π_∞`, a place),\nNOT a functor: it maps objects of `Arch` to the set `ℝ`, with no\naction on morphisms. Only `τ` (below) is a functor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.MotivicMassMeasure.divisorWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.MotivicMassMeasure.divisorWeight","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Codimension/weight `d_i` of each exceptional divisor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.MotivicMassMeasure.divisorClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.MotivicMassMeasure.divisorClass","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L64-L64","doc":"The class `[E_i^∘]` of the smooth open part of each exceptional divisor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.MotivicMassMeasure.numDivisors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.MotivicMassMeasure.numDivisors","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L62-L62","doc":"Number of exceptional divisors produced by the reduction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.MotivicMassMeasure.totalMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.MotivicMassMeasure.totalMass","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The measure of the whole arc space (= total motivic mass). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.MotivicMassMeasure.K0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.MotivicMassMeasure.K0","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L58-L58","doc":"Ambient Grothendieck ring (target of the measure). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.MotivicMassMeasure.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.MotivicMassMeasure.mk","kind":"ctor","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.MotivicMassMeasure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.MotivicMassMeasure","kind":"structure","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L51-L66","doc":"The **motivic mass measure** `μ` on the arc space `L(X)`.\n\nRecords the total motivic volume as a sum over exceptional\ndivisors of the Gröbner-Shirshov reduction:\n`∫ dμ = ∑_i [E_i^∘] · L^{-d_i}`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:motivic-mass-measure","label":"def:motivic-mass-measure","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/motivic-mass-measure.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.GrothendieckRingOfVarieties.classOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.GrothendieckRingOfVarieties.classOf","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Class map `[·] : Var → Ring`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.GrothendieckRingOfVarieties.lefschetz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.GrothendieckRingOfVarieties.lefschetz","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L47-L47","doc":"The Lefschetz motive `L = [A¹]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.GrothendieckRingOfVarieties.Ring","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.GrothendieckRingOfVarieties.Ring","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L45-L45","doc":"Underlying ring carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.GrothendieckRingOfVarieties.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.GrothendieckRingOfVarieties.mk","kind":"ctor","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.GrothendieckRingOfVarieties","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.GrothendieckRingOfVarieties","kind":"structure","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MotivesArchimedean.lean#L39-L49","doc":"Abstract Grothendieck ring of varieties `K_0(Var_k)`.\n\nCarries the Lefschetz motive `L = [A¹]` and admits the\nlocalization `M = K_0(Var)[L^{-1}]` used by motivic integration. ","signatureChunk":0}]}